            "repere": "Intertitre · Most of the coffee for sale in retail …",
            "text": "Most of the coffee for sale in retail stores and coffee shops is a mix-and-match of beans from various plants and countries around the world. With blends, you might get beans mixed with pesticide-soaked beans. It’s also possible you can get premium dark roast beans mixed with under-dried, toxin-filled lighter roast beans.<br><br>Single-Origin coffee ensures you’re getting what you pay for - and nothing you don’t want in your coffee. <span style=\"font-weight:700\">Every bag of this coffee, however, is guaranteed single origin. </span> Each bag is filled with beans from the same farm, the same plant, and the same roast profile.<br><br>",
